   *   #3    12,517  (no four headings at all)
   *   #4    11,191  (no four headings at all)
   *
   * #2's `What I concluded` held six headings that were the deliverable the issue
   * asked for. #3 and #4 moved the deliverable outside the four parts and barely
   * wrote the headings -- so the contract never decided where the artifact goes.
   *
   * Anchored sentences by part, #2's engineer (same regex style as the earlier
   * measurement): `How I know` 10/11 = 91%, `What you could not establish` 6/13 =
   * 46%. So the part worth narrowing is `How I know`, and the part whose ratio must
   * not be traded away is the one that goes missing -- which is why that one gets a
   * floor and no ceiling. Narrowing `How I know` lowers its own ratio by shrinking
   * the denominator; that is not a regression, and the metric to compare across this
   * change is anchored claims per report, not their share.
